  "body": "Implements P1-S2 (#1279): explicit target control, owned sessions, end-to-end WhatIf, fixed endpoint requests, checked HTTP/service bindings, and durable command journals. HTTP requests now require the validated process to own the advertised listener; mismatched, unreadable or conflicting ownership fails closed before sending authentication or prompt data.\n\nValidation at bc16ccff3601fabeeb783f41b52360ef5851838a: Linux 1777/1777; strict manifest 184/184; existing Ruff F821 delta 0. Native PS5.1/7: 26/26 normal and 38/38 focused checks per runtime. Old H3 reproduces the wrong-listener leak with owned dummy-key wire fixtures. Fresh independent Codex CLI review3 approved, closed all three prior finding classes, and found no new issues: https://github.com/ducthangho/tra-luat/issues/1279#issuecomment-6720089491 . Original H3 review and finding history remain preserved.\n\nScope: three new files, 1773 additions; S1 unchanged. Offline control only; S3 packaging and optional Playwright integration remain later work. Windows CI is excluded by owner; no runtime activation or deployment. H4 PR CI, connector review, merge and land checks remain pending.\n",
